//@version=6
// WAR FORMATION E94b -- INDEPENDENT REPLICATION OF E94. RENUMBERED AFTER THE FACT.
//
// ██ NUMBERING NOTE, WRITTEN AFTER THE RUN. This file was authored and this backtest was run as
// "E94" by a concurrent session, ~20 minutes after ANOTHER concurrent session committed its own
// E94 (b15e5e8, pine/e94-e93-long-only.pine, resultId 01M1V6H407ST3XEWGRC8H2KC53) executing the
// SAME E93 queue item 1. Both sessions took War Formation's rotation slot and both spent a credit
// on the same question. The collision was found on rebase, not before.
//
// This branch is renumbered to E94b rather than leaving a fourth colliding pair in the log (E79,
// E80, E81 already collide). The other E94 was committed first and keeps the number. Its entry is
// the primary record of the experiment; the E94b entry in EXPERIMENT-LOG.md records only what
// this run adds that is not already there -- the exact replication itself, and the significance
// test on the axis the board already uses.
//
// Everything below this line is the ORIGINAL pre-registration, written and saved to disk BEFORE
// the credit was spent and left unedited so the predictions can be scored against the result.
// WAR FORMATION E94 -- E80/E93's 1h-STRUCTURE CASCADE, LONG-ONLY, ON THE FULL 6-YEAR ARCHIVE.
//
// PARENT: E93 (resultId 01M1V526XR04BWHC7Q0ZHE5CEE, strategyId 01M1SMXCYQ9KD43GRJJJ0TN7N4),
// which ran pine/e80-15m-native-1h-structure.pine bidirectionally over
// 2020-08-19 -> 2026-09-01 and returned PF 1.08806654 on 147 reported trades, with the LONG
// leg net +$2,714.31 and the SHORT leg net -$1,801.00.
//
// THIS IS E93 QUEUE ITEM 1, PRE-REGISTERED THERE VERBATIM: "Re-run this same construction
// LONG-ONLY on the full 6-year archive (mechanically delete goShort / the short
// strategy.entry, the way e50a/e50b did for the 1m track) to see whether dropping the
// now-established-weak short leg improves PF/DD relative to this bidirectional full-archive
// number (1.08806654 / 147 trades)."
//
// BINDING (E17 / HARD LESSON 16): the ONLY change from e80-15m-native-1h-structure.pine is the
// deletion of the short leg -- `goShort`, its `strategy.entry`, and the now-dead
// `strategy.position_size < 0` exit block. shieldUsd ($2,000), rr (2.0), coilK (0.85),
// velK (0.8), maxBars (288), greenBull/greenBear, the time gate, the witching ban, the whole-
// number band, the 1h structure tier and the latch order are all byte-identical to the parent.
// The backtest window is byte-identical to E93's (2020-08-19 -> 2026-09-01). Two variables are
// therefore NOT being changed at once: E93 changed the window against E80; E94 changes the leg
// against E93.
//
// THE OCCUPANCY CONFOUND IS THE POINT OF THE TEST, NOT A HIDDEN DEFECT (HARD LESSONS 24/28/29).
// The parent runs pyramiding=1 with a `flat` guard, so every short entry BLOCKS any long signal
// that fires while the short is open. Deleting the short leg therefore cannot be modelled as
// "E93 minus the short rows": the long population is free to GROW above E93's 43. Whether it
// does, and whether the added longs are better or worse than the 43 already recorded, is
// exactly what this run measures. It is declared here in advance so the trade count is read as
// a result rather than as a surprise.
//
// PRE-RUN AUDIT
//   R floor (HARD LESSON 3): shieldUsd $2,000 against E93's own traded entry-price range on
//     this exact window ($10,117.50 - $121,267, read from get_trades on the parent) is
//     1.65% - 19.77% of price. Clears the 0.8% floor across the entire archive.
//   Stop placement (HARD LESSON 5): unchanged, risk-defined per the ALCM spec, not at the
//     signal level.
//   Leg reporting (HARD LESSON 6): only one leg exists by construction; this run must be
//     described as LONG-ONLY and therefore an INTERIM state under the standing both-directions
//     requirement, never as a finished bidirectional result.
//   Latch order (HARD LESSON 8): unchanged.
//   Redundancy (HARD LESSON 18): no term added.
//
// REGISTERED PREDICTIONS (HARD LESSON 17), BEFORE RUNNING:
//   P1. PF should IMPROVE on E93's 1.08806654, because a net-negative leg is being removed.
//       This is close to arithmetic and is therefore NOT the interesting output.
//   P2. The interesting output is the LONG TRADE COUNT. If it stays near 43, the shorts were
//       rarely blocking longs and the long leg's own per-year profile (below) is unchanged.
//       If it rises materially, the added longs are a genuinely new, previously unobservable
//       population and must be phase-decomposed before the headline PF is believed.
//   P3. THE PHASE PREDICTION, which is the one that matters. A free get_trades decomposition of
//       E93 (performed this cycle, before this run) shows the parent's LONG leg is not broadly
//       profitable at all: its entire net comes from calendar 2020. By entry year --
//         2020: 7 trades, +$2,532.70   2021: 5, -$510.09   2022: 2, +$303.40
//         2023: 7,   +$743.59          2024: 7,  -$52.56   2025: 8, +$712.40
//         2026: 7, -$1,015.13
//       -- so the 4.5-month 2020 stub (+$2,532.70) alone exceeds the whole leg's +$2,714.31 net
//       by all but $181.61 across the other 36 trades. PREDICTION: this run's long-only PF will
//       show the SAME concentration, i.e. removing 2020 will leave a PF at or below ~1.0 on the
//       remaining trades. If so, "long-only-viable" as E93 phrased it does not survive a phase
//       decomposition (HARD LESSON 54) and must be withdrawn.
//
// RESULT, VERDICT and KEEP/REJECT are recorded in EXPERIMENT-LOG.md and
// war-formation/results/backtests.json after this run completes. No metric is hand-written.
strategy("War Formation E94 15m 1h-structure LONG ONLY full archive", overlay=true,
     pyramiding=1, process_orders_on_close=true,
     commission_type=strategy.commission.percent, commission_value=0.05,
     initial_capital=10000,
     default_qty_type=strategy.percent_of_equity, default_qty_value=100,
     margin_long=100, margin_short=100)

greenBull = input.int(4,     "Green 1h candles for BULL")
greenBear = input.int(2,     "Green 1h candles at or below for BEAR")
skipOpen  = input.int(60,    "Skip first N minutes of 6h block")
skipClose = input.int(60,    "Skip last N minutes of 6h block")
coilK     = input.float(0.85,"Coil: atrFast < atrSlow * K")
velK      = input.float(0.8, "Velocity: min reclaim as multiple of atrSlow")
midLo     = input.float(400, "Whole-number middles low")
midHi     = input.float(600, "Whole-number middles high")
etOffset  = input.int(-4,    "ET offset from UTC")
witchOn   = input.bool(true, "Ban longs in witching hour 1-4am ET")
shieldUsd = input.float(2000,"THE SHIELD: fixed dollar gap to liquidation")
rr        = input.float(2.0, "Reward:risk")
maxBars   = input.int(288,   "Max bars in trade -- three days of 15m")

MS6H = 21600000
MS1H = 3600000

b6  = math.floor(time / MS6H)
b1h = math.floor(time / MS1H)

new6  = b6  != b6[1]
new1h = b1h != b1h[1]

var float h1o     = na
var int   grnCur  = 0
var int   cntCur  = 0
var int   grnPrev = 0
var int   cntPrev = 0

if new6
    grnPrev := grnCur
    cntPrev := cntCur
    grnCur  := 0
    cntCur  := 0

if new1h
    if not na(h1o)
        cntCur := cntCur + 1
        if close[1] > h1o
            grnCur := grnCur + 1
    h1o := open

regimeReady = cntPrev >= 5
bullRegime  = regimeReady and grnPrev >= greenBull
bearRegime  = regimeReady and grnPrev <= greenBear

minsIn    = (time - b6 * MS6H) / 60000
timeGate  = minsIn >= skipOpen and minsIn <= (360 - skipClose)

h1Bull = not na(h1o) and close > h1o
h1Bear = not na(h1o) and close < h1o

var float c1hh = na
var float c1hl = na
var float p1hh = na
var float p1hl = na

if new1h
    p1hh := c1hh
    p1hl := c1hl
    c1hh := high
    c1hl := low
else
    c1hh := na(c1hh) ? high : math.max(c1hh, high)
    c1hl := na(c1hl) ? low  : math.min(c1hl, low)

brokeBelow = not na(p1hl) and c1hl < p1hl
brokeAbove = not na(p1hh) and c1hh > p1hh

atrFast = ta.atr(1)
atrSlow = ta.atr(2)
coiled  = not na(atrSlow) and atrSlow > 0 and atrFast < atrSlow * coilK
coilPrev = coiled[1]
velMin   = na(atrSlow) ? na : atrSlow * velK

sub      = close - math.floor(close / 1000) * 1000
inMiddle = sub >= midLo and sub <= midHi

hUTC     = math.floor(time / MS1H) % 24
hET      = (hUTC + etOffset + 24) % 24
witching = hET >= 1 and hET < 4
longBan  = witchOn and witching

longTrig  = not na(p1hl) and not na(velMin) and ta.crossover(close, p1hl)  and (close - p1hl) >= velMin

// SHORT LEG DELETED -- this is the single change from the parent.
goLong  = bullRegime and timeGate and h1Bull and brokeBelow and coilPrev and not inMiddle and not longBan and longTrig

var float slPx   = na
var float tpPx   = na
var int   barsIn = 0

flat = strategy.position_size == 0

if flat and goLong
    strategy.entry("L", strategy.long)
    slPx   := close - shieldUsd
    tpPx   := close + shieldUsd * rr
    barsIn := 0

if strategy.position_size > 0
    strategy.exit("LX", from_entry="L", stop=slPx, limit=tpPx)
    barsIn := barsIn + 1

if barsIn >= maxBars and strategy.position_size != 0
    strategy.close_all()
    barsIn := 0

plot(goLong ? 1 : 0, title="LongSignal")
